# UI change safety (Persona)

Current brand tokens live in `frontend/src/styles/globals.css`:
- Day accent `#002fa7` (Klein blue)
- Night accent `#e11d48` (crimson)

## Cursor "Revert conversation" (most common wipe)

Reverting a chat restores that chat's file checkpoint onto disk. It does **not** remove git commits, but it can put teal `#1f6b5a` back in the working tree.

Recovery (repo root):

```powershell
.\restore-ui.ps1
```

Then reload editors from disk and hard-refresh the browser.

Agents recovering from teal may `git restore --source=HEAD --` the paths listed in `restore-ui.ps1`. Do not restore a pre-Persona commit unless the user explicitly asks.

## Never do without an explicit user request that lists paths

- Restoring "original" / "before redesign" UI from an old commit
- Replacing truncated CSS with a full pre-Persona `globals.css`

## After any UI write touching theme/shell

Confirm day `--accent: #002fa7` on disk. If `#1f6b5a` reappears, tell the user and offer `.\restore-ui.ps1`.

## PowerShell scripts

`dev.ps1` must stay ASCII-only. Prefer `api:` labels over `[api]` tags.
